Cmn1=Event Scheduler 2 v1.2.0\\\\\\Revision History\\================\\
Cmn2=\\v1.2.0\\------\\-Added a Version number at the top of the schedule||1
Cmn3=file. All schedules saved by module v 1.2.0 will contain #2 in the||1
Cmn4=first line. \\-Added a Flags Field,Last Modified date/time field,||1
Cmn5=and User Data Field to each event.\\-User Data must be a single||1
Cmn6=line entry of less than 50 characters. \\-Current flags are R =||1
Cmn7=read-only, H = hidden. \\-Hidden Events will not display on the||1
Cmn8=scheduler output.\\-Read Only Events cannot be modified but can||1
Cmn9=be suspended\activated. Suspending a RO event updates the LastModified||1
Cmn10=Field.\\-Added a Read-only digital output   \\\\v1.1.2\\------\\
Cmn11=-Fixed bug where scheduler data file was only being written partially||1
Cmn12=to disk in rare cases. This would result in a loss of schedule data.
Cmn13=||1(As part of this fix, there will be at least a 5 second delay after||1
Cmn14=a request to Save before the file is actually written to disk).\\
Cmn15=-Suspend flag is now saved as part of scheduler data file (file||1
Cmn16=will be automatically saved after Suspend flag is changed)\\-Fixed||1
Cmn17=bug where pressing Save/Revert caused the current "Edit Event" to||1
Cmn18=jump back to the first event in the file.\\\\v1.1.1\\------\\-initial||1
Cmn19=release\\\\\\Description\\===========\\\\The Event Scheduler 2 module||1
Cmn20=differs from but does not replace the original Event \\Scheduler||1
Cmn21=module. The original module allowed you to schedule events to occur||1
Cmn22=on\\particular days of the year, and allowed for repeating events||1
Cmn23=which could repeat\\at specified intervals.\\\\The Event Scheduler||1
Cmn24=2 module allows you to schedule events to occur on particular\\days||1
Cmn25=of the week in particular months. That is, you can create an event||1
Cmn26=that occurs\\each Monday, Wednesday, and Friday only during the||1
Cmn27=months of June, July, and August.\\In addition, event times can||1
Cmn28=be absolute (i.e. based on AM or PM) or astronomic\\(i.e. relative||1
Cmn29=to sunrise or sunset).\\\\Another important distinction between||1
Cmn30=the Event Scheduler and Event Scheduler 2 is\\that in this version,||1
Cmn31=event data is stored on a file residing either on compact \\flash||1
Cmn32=or (in the near future) in the processor's internal flash. This||1
Cmn33=means that\\events must first be created using a PC to generate||1
Cmn34=the event file. This can be\\done manually using a text editor,||1
Cmn35=or using an application that supports Event\\Scheduling such as||1
Cmn36=D3 Pro or Application Builder (v1.3 or above).\\\\Once the event||1
Cmn37=schedule file has been uploaded to the control system, the events||1
Cmn38=may\\be modified using a touchpanel provided the Read-only or Hidden||1
Cmn39=flag is not set. Events cannot be renamed, removed or added in\\
Cmn40=this manner. Read-only events cannot be modified, but can be suspended.
Cmn41=||1Hidden events will not be displayed and can only be viewed or modified||1
Cmn42=by editing \\the schedule text file.\\\\Following is the syntax||1
Cmn43=of the event file:\\\\  <event number>,<name>,<timebase>,<time offset(in||1
Cmn44=minutes)>,<day flags>,<month flags>,<suspend flag>*,<flags>*,<last||1
Cmn45=modified date/time>*,<user data>*\\  <event number>,<name>,<timebase>,<time||1
Cmn46=offset(in minutes)>,<day flags>,<month flags>,<suspend flag>*,<flags>*,<last||1
Cmn47=modified date/time>*,<user data>*\\  ...\\  <event number>,<name>,<timebase>,<tim
Cmn48=e offset(in minutes)>,<day flags>,<month flags>,<suspend flag>*,<flags>*,<last||1
Cmn49=modified date/time>*,<user data>*\\\\\\* indicates an optional field||1
Cmn50=(note that prior entries must be included - See examples below)\\
Cmn51=\\where:\\\\  <event number> = integer from 1 to 250 (you can leave||1
Cmn52=gaps but it is inefficient)\\\\  <name> = the event name (from 1||1
Cmn53=to 30 characters)\\\\  <timebase> = integer from 0 - 3:\\||7
Cmn54=||:0 = AM\\                 1 = PM\\                 2 =||1
Cmn55=Sunrise\\                 3 = Sunset\\\\  <time offset> = the number||1
Cmn56=of minutes before/after the time base. For absolute events\\||4
Cmn57=||>(AM/PM) these should be positive values ranging from||1
Cmn58=0 to 719 (11 hours\\                  and 59 minutes). For Astronomic||1
Cmn59=events, these can be positive or negative\\                  and||1
Cmn60=should range from -360 to +360 (plus sign not needed for positive\\
Cmn61=||Bnumbers).\\\\  <day flags> = a series of 7 characters||1
Cmn62=that indicate whether or not this event is valid\\||>
Cmn63=||2for a given day of the week. Days go in order from Sunday to Saturday,||1
Cmn64=\\                and an 'X' is used to indicate that the day is||1
Cmn65=valid, and a '-' is used\\                to indicate that the day||1
Cmn66=is invalid. Here are some examples:\\\\                  XXXXXXX||1
Cmn67=||1<-- event is valid each day of the week\\                  -XXXXX-
Cmn68=||2<-- event is valid Monday through Friday only\\||?
Cmn69=||3X-----X  <-- event is valid weekends only\\||B
Cmn70=-X-X-X-  <-- event is valid Monday, Wednesday, Friday\\\\  <month||1
Cmn71=flags> = a series of 12 characters that indicate whether or not||1
Cmn72=this event is \\                  valid for a given month of the||1
Cmn73=year. Months go in order from January to \\                  December,||1
Cmn74=and an 'X' is used to indicate that the month is valid, and \\||2
Cmn75=||@a '-' is used to indicate that the month is invalid.
Cmn76=||1Here are some examples:\\\\                  XXXXXXXXXXXX  <--||1
Cmn77=event is valid each month of the year\\                  XXX----
Cmn78=--XXX  <-- event is valid Jan-Mar and Oct-Dec\\||A
Cmn79=||1---XXXXXX---  <-- event is valid April through September\\\\  <suspend||1
Cmn80=flag> (optional) = integer from 0-1:\\                   	||6
Cmn81=0 = NOT suspended\\		              1 = suspended\\		\\			      If||1
Cmn82=this flag is omitted, event will be assumed to be not suspended||1
Cmn83=(i.e. event will be active)\\  \\  <flags field> (optional) = characters||1
Cmn84=H or R\\			     H = Hidden event\\			     R = Read-only event\\	
Cmn85=If this field is omitted, event will be assumed to be shown with||1
Cmn86=Read\Write privileges\\  \\  <last modified date/time> (optional)||1
Cmn87== a 16 character string with standard format of mmddyyyy:hhmmss||1
Cmn88=\\                                         This field may be left||1
Cmn89=blank or omitted. Information does not display to a touchpanel.\\
Cmn90=\\  <user data> (optional) = must be a single line entry (No Carriage||1
Cmn91=Return\Line Feed) of less than 50 characters. Information does not||1
Cmn92=display to a touchpanel. \\  \\Here is what an actual file might||1
Cmn93=look like:\\\\  1,Wake Up,0,450,-XXXXX-,XXXXXXXXXXXX\\  2,Goodnight,1,660,-
Cmn94=XXXXX-,XXXXXXXXXXXX\\  3,Sprinklers On,3,240,-X-X-X-,---XXXXXX--
Cmn95=-,0\\  4,Sprinklers Off,3,280,-X-X-X-,---XXXXXX---,0\\  5,Vacation,1,360,xxxxxxx,
Cmn96=xxxxxxxxxxxx,1,R\\  6,Maintenance,0,180,------x,xxxxxxxxxxxx,0,H\\
Cmn97=||27,Security,3,0,xxxxxxx,xxxxxxxxxxxx,0,,,Scheduled event for south||1
Cmn98=walkway lighting\\\\which can be interpreted as:\\\\  Wake Up: occurs||1
Cmn99=each weekday at 7:30 AM (450 minutes after midnight)\\  Goodnight:
Cmn100=||1occurs each weekday at 11:00 PM (660 minutes after noon)\\  Sprinklers||1
Cmn101=On: occurs 4 hours after sunset on Mon, Wed, Fri during the months||1
Cmn102=Apr - Sep\\  Sprinklers Off: occurs 4 hours, 40 minutes after sunset||1
Cmn103=on Mon, Wed, Fri during the months Apr - Sep\\  Vacation: occurs||1
Cmn104=daily at 6:00 PM. This event is currently suspended and will not||1
Cmn105=run until activated. It is Read-only but can be activated\suspend.
Cmn106=\\  Maintenance: occurs at 3:00 AM on Saturday. This event is hidden||1
Cmn107=from the user and cannot be viewed from a touchpanel\\  Security:
Cmn108=||1occurs daily at sunset\\\\\\INPUT DESCRIPTIONS\\==================\\
Cmn109=\\  For better clarity, the inputs and outputs have been grouped||1
Cmn110=below by general functionality:\\\\  ENABLE AND DISABLE\\  ==================\\
Cmn111=||2Enable (D)  - enables the scheduler (scheduled events will fire||1
Cmn112=at the appropriate time)\\  Disable (D) - disables the scheduler||1
Cmn113=(no events will fire)\\  Enable/Disable (D) - toggles between enabled||1
Cmn114=and disabled.\\\\  SELECTING THE "EDIT" EVENT\\  ==========================\\
Cmn115=||2Edit_First_Event (D) - sets the edit event pointer to the first||1
Cmn116=event in the list\\  Edit_Prev_Event (D)  - sets the edit event||1
Cmn117=pointer to the previous event in the list\\  Edit_Last_Event (D)||1
Cmn118=||1- sets the edit event pointer to the next event in the list\\||2
Cmn119=Edit_Last_Event (D)  - sets the edit event pointer to the last event||1
Cmn120=in the list\\\\  SUSPENDING THE "EDIT" EVENT\\  ===========================\\
Cmn121=||2Suspend (D) - suspends the current event (will not fire).\\  Resume||1
Cmn122=||1(D) - resumes the current event (will fire). \\\\  NOTE: changing||1
Cmn123=the Suspend flag for any event will cause the entire scheduler file||1
Cmn124=to be \\        written to disk automatically.\\\\  SAVING/CANCELING||1
Cmn125=CHANGES TO THE "EDIT" EVENT\\  ============================================\\
Cmn126=||2Save   (D) - saves the "edit" event to disk\\  Revert (D) - cancels||1
Cmn127=any changes made to the "edit" event, and reverts back to the last||1
Cmn128=saved copy\\\\  MODIFYING THE "EDIT" EVENT'S TIME\\  ============================
Cmn129======\\  Hour+   (D) - increments the "edit" event's hour\\  Hour-
Cmn130=||3(D) - decrements the "edit" event's hour\\  Minute+ (D) - increments||1
Cmn131=the "edit" event's minute\\  Minute- (D) - decrements the "edit"||1
Cmn132=event's minute\\  AM      (D) - sets the "edit"  event's timebase||1
Cmn133=to AM\\  PM      (D) - sets the "edit"  event's timebase to PM\\
Cmn134=||2Sunrise (D) - sets the "edit"  event's timebase to Sunrise\\||2
Cmn135=Sunset  (D) - sets the "edit"  event's timebase to Sunset\\\\  MODIFYING||1
Cmn136=THE "EDIT" EVENT'S VALID DAYS OF THE WEEK\\  ====================================
Cmn137================\\  Sunday_On/Off   (D) - toggles whether the "edit"||1
Cmn138=event is valid on Sundays\\  ...\\  Saturday_On/Off (D) - toggles||1
Cmn139=whether the "edit" event is valid on Saturdays\\\\  MODIFYING THE||1
Cmn140="EDIT" EVENT'S VALID MONTHS\\  =========================================\\
Cmn141=||2January_On/Off  (D) - toggles whether the "edit" event is valid||1
Cmn142=in January\\  ...\\  December_On/Off (D) - toggles whether the "edit"||1
Cmn143=event is valid in December\\\\  WHERE TO GET THE SCHEDULER DATA||1
Cmn144=FROM ("{{" and "}}" are used to hide inputs from D3Pro and AppBuilder)\\
Cmn145=||2====================================\\  {{filename$}} (S) - the||1
Cmn146=name of the file that contains the scheduler data (includes path).
Cmn147=||1Be sure\\                      to use a two backslashes in order||1
Cmn148=to achieve a single backslash character. For files on\\||9
Cmn149=||=Compact Flash, the root node is "CF0". For files on||1
Cmn150=the NVRAM disk, root node\\                      is "NVRAM".\\||2
Cmn151={{Morning_Hour}} (A) - the sunrise hour for the current day (comes||1
Cmn152=from the Astronomical Clock symbol)\\  {{Morning_Min}}  (A) - the||1
Cmn153=sunrise minute for the current day (comes from the Astronomical||1
Cmn154=Clock symbol)\\  {{Night_Hour}}   (A) - the sunset hour for the||1
Cmn155=current day (comes from the Astronomical Clock symbol)\\  {{Night_Min}}||1
Cmn156=||3(A) - the sunset minute for the current day (comes from the Astronomical||1
Cmn157=Clock symbol)\\\\OUTPUT DESCRIPTIONS\\===================\\\\  ENABLE||1
Cmn158=AND DISABLE\\  ==================\\  Enabled (D) - high if the Scheduler||1
Cmn159=is currently enabled\\\\  THE CURRENT "EDIT" EVENT\\  ==========================\\
Cmn160=||2Edit_Event_Name$  (S) - the name of the currently selected "edit"||1
Cmn161=event\\  Edit_Event_Time$  (S) - the time (including time base)||1
Cmn162=of the currently selected "edit" event\\  Edit_Event_Number (A)||1
Cmn163=- the number (index) of the "edit" event. Comes from file, so is||1
Cmn164=not\\                          necessarily in sequence.\\\\  SUSPENDED||1
Cmn165="EDIT" EVENTS\\  ===========================\\  Suspend_fb (D) -
Cmn166=||1high if the "edit" event is currently suspended\\\\  READONLY "EDIT"||1
Cmn167=EVENTS\\  ===========================\\  ReadOnly_fb (D) - high||1
Cmn168=if the "edit" event is currently Read-only\\\\  THE "EDIT" EVENT'S||1
Cmn169=TIME\\  =================================\\  AM_fb      (D) - high||1
Cmn170=if the "edit" event's timebase is AM\\  PM_fb      (D) - high if||1
Cmn171=the "edit" event's timebase is PM\\  Sunrise_fb (D) - high if the||1
Cmn172="edit" event's timebase is Sunrise\\  Sunset_fb  (D) - high if the||1
Cmn173="edit" event's timebase is Sunset\\\\  THE "EDIT" EVENT'S VALID||1
Cmn174=DAYS OF THE WEEK\\  ===================================================\\
Cmn175=||2Sunday_On/Off_fb   (D) - high if the "edit" event is valid on||1
Cmn176=Sundays\\  ...\\  Saturday_On/Off_fb (D) - high if the "edit" event||1
Cmn177=is valid on Saturday\\\\  THE "EDIT" EVENT'S VALID MONTHS\\  ====================
Cmn178======================\\  January_On/Off_fb  (D) - high if the "edit"||1
Cmn179=event is valid in January\\  ...\\  December_On/Off_fb (D) - high||1
Cmn180=if the "edit" event is valid in December\\\\  EVENT ACTIVATION\\
Cmn181=||2================\\  Message$      (S) - a text message offering||1
Cmn182=information about what is happening\\  Event_1_due   (D) - pulses||1
Cmn183=when event 1 is due. Tie this to other logic to make this event||1
Cmn184=do something.\\  ...\\  Event_250_due (D) - pulses when event 250||1
Cmn185=is due. Tie this to other logic to make this event do something.
Cmn186=\\\\\\#BEGIN_CONDITIONALS\\\\#D,Enabled,Enabled,Disabled\\\\#END_CONDITIONALS
